sequenceDiagram
  %% Source: crates/shipyard-app/src/device_login.rs (OAuth PKCE, RFC 7636) and crates/shipyard-app/src/pkce.rs.
  actor Person
  participant UI as React UI
  participant Shell as Tauri shell
  participant Browser as Web browser
  participant OR as openrouter.ai
  participant Keychain as OS keychain

  Person->>UI: Click Sign in on the OpenRouter row
  UI->>Shell: providers_openrouter_sign_in(click)
  Note over Shell: One sign-in at a time.<br/>Make a random verifier and state.<br/>Listen on 127.0.0.1, random port
  Shell->>Browser: Open /auth?callback_url=127.0.0.1/callback/state&code_challenge=S256(verifier)
  Person->>OR: Approve in the browser
  OR->>Browser: Redirect to the callback with code
  Browser->>Shell: GET /callback/state?code=...
  alt path and state match, code is plain text
    Shell-->>Browser: 200, close this tab
  else empty connection
    Note over Shell: Close it and wait on
  else other request
    Shell-->>Browser: 400, the sign-in ends
  end
  alt Cancel or 10 minutes
    UI->>Shell: providers_openrouter_cancel()
    Shell-->>UI: Error, nothing stored
  end
  Shell->>OR: POST /api/v1/auth/keys (code, code_verifier)
  OR-->>Shell: key
  Shell->>Keychain: Store the key (provider OpenRouter)
  Note over Shell: The key reaches no log, no file and no error text
  Shell-->>UI: Provider row, signed in
